  "id": "COMPOUND:19638 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between 3,5-Dimethoxy-9,10-Dihydrophenanthrene-2,7-Diol and the CD276 antigen, as this compound acts as a target for multiple compounds that ultimately inhibit CD276. The compound is involved in the target of three distinct molecules—Phlorigidoside C, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and Tamarixinin B—all of which are implicated in the inhibition of CD276. This indicates that the compound may function as a common intermediate or modulator in the pathways leading to CD276 inhibition. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, biologically plausible mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets implies that the compound may exert its effects through diverse molecular mechanisms, potentially involving different cellular pathways or interactions.",
